  <revision rev="1" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>0dcb593cdea7783d61c3f019b65c7e62</srcmd5>
    <version>0.44.2</version>
    <time>1786026325</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>New package: rtk 0.44.2 (Rust Token Killer)

Command line proxy for the shell commands coding agents run most often. It
executes the wrapped command, filters and compresses the output, and prints
only the informative part, cutting the tokens the result costs in an LLM
context window. Ships filters for build systems, linters, test runners,
version control and cloud tooling, and passes unrecognised commands through
unchanged.

Apache-2.0, single Rust binary, upstream https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk

Two downstream patches, both submitted upstream:
- rtk-unbundle-sqlite.patch links the system SQLite instead of the copy
  statically linked in from libsqlite3-sys, so the binary is covered by the
  distribution SQLite updates (upstream PR 3446).
- rtk-no-deny-warnings.patch stops rustc warnings being promoted to errors;
  the distribution rustc moves independently of the version floor upstream
  builds against (upstream PR 3447).

Telemetry is opt-in only and stays off unless explicitly enabled.

Verified on aarch64 (local) and x86_64 (OBS): builds green, test suite
2584 passed / 0 failed, rpmlint 0 errors 0 warnings 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1369751</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>d01345493a7983c023408f37bf7e2788</srcmd5>
    <version>0.45.0</version>
    <time>1786461018</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to version 0.45.0.

Upstream adds transparent hook support for the Mistral Vibe CLI and
multiline block rewriting, and fixes the Copilot hook handling: rtk no
longer lets Copilot silently decide permission on unconfigured commands,
and it self-heals a stale dual-schema hook config while touching only its
own legacy camelCase entry.

Also corrects the License tag. The binary statically links the vendored
crates, and the linked graph (127 of the 186 vendored crates, per
cargo tree --offline -p rtk -e normal) carries MPL-2.0 (colored,
option-ext), Unicode-3.0 (the ICU/zerovec crates), ISC (rustls-webpki,
untrusted, ring), CDLA-Permissive-2.0 (webpki-roots), BSD-3-Clause
(subtle) and MIT on top of rtk's own Apache-2.0. The reasoning is recorded
in a Legal-Review-Notice comment above the tag.

Built locally on aarch64: 2655 tests pass, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings /
0 badness. Both downstream patches still apply unchanged; upstream PRs
3446 and 3447 are still open.</comment>
    <requestid>1370422</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>9fd95dd614fc30e798e1c6bc4f209dc0</srcmd5>
    <version>0.46.0</version>
