    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.46.0 (upstream release 2026-08-26).

Upstream tags release candidates as GitHub releases and they sort above stable
-- dev-0.46.1-rc.367 is NEWER by date than v0.46.0. Target picked by the
prerelease flag, not tag order.

Both downstream patches are still required and still apply at --fuzz=0: the
upstream PRs they were sent as (3446 unbundle-sqlite, 3447 no-deny-warnings)
are both still open.

Verified: 2728 tests pass / 0 fail, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness,
source_validator clean, spec-cleaner no-diff. The RPM still carries
Requires: libsqlite3.so.0 (sqlite is not re-bundled) and rtk-debuginfo is
9.8 MB (release profile strip is still disabled).

Licence re-derived on this re-vendor with cargo tree -e normal: 193 crates
vendored, 134 linked. The License tag is unchanged -- every mandatory licence
(MPL-2.0, Unicode-3.0, ISC, CDLA-Permissive-2.0, BSD-3-Clause) is already named
and every OR expression is satisfied by Apache-2.0 or MIT. Only the stale counts
in the Legal-Review-Notice comment were refreshed.</comment>
